      {
        "position": 6,
        "title": "Smells amazing",
        "text": "When I first got this spray, my first thought was, why so pricey? But I definitely get it now. This is a true limited ingredient disinfectant spray. 99.982% water and 0.018% hypochlorous acid. That's it. This is an extremely gentle disinfectant that doesn't require rinsing. You just have to clean first and then use this spray after.When sprayed, it doesn't have much of a scent, but if you smell the open bottle then it smells very much like a hotel pool. Which I honestly love that smell. It smells clean.I can't really speak to how effective it is because I don't take cultures from my countertops and other surfaces. But I trust that it is.The benefits of using this type of cleaner compared to other disinfectants is how much more gentle it is. It's not corrosive, safe for food surfaces and doesn't require rinsing. It is really great for daily use to wipe down surfaces around the house without leaving heavy chemical residue everywhere.I honestly like this stuff a lot. I think that I'm going to keep a bottle of it around the house from here on out because I like the thought of keeping surfaces disinfected without using harsh chemicals that require rinsing and leave residue behind.",
