      {
        "position": 8,
        "title": "Finally a cleaner I don't stress about",
        "text": "Wondercide's disinfectant spray kinda snuck up on me. I grabbed it mostly outta curiosity since I got a dog who licks literally everything and I was nervous bout using anything harsh around him. First use was on his food bowl and some chew toys and I just... didn't stress at all. No rinsing needed, no fumes, no weird chemical smell. Just sprayed and let it air dry. That alone was worth it for me.Quality-wise this stuff holds up real good. It kills a solid list of germs including MRSA, Salmonella and even SARS-CoV-2 which was honestly more than I expected from something made outta salt water and electricity. Used it all over, kitchen counters bathroom sink, even the litter box area and it handled all of it without leaving any residue or bleaching anything out. My countertops still look fine and my fabrics haven't had any discoloring issues either.Value for money, yeah its competitive. You not paying for fancy fragrance or dye fillers, just functional clean. Design of the bottle is pretty basic nothing flashy but the spray nozzle works good and doesn't clog up. Functionality overall is where this thing really shines considering how many surfaces it covers without needing different products for each spot. Solid buy for busy households or anyone with pets kids or just general germ anxiety.",
